  "headline": "The model is competitive on MAE yet flags almost no losses, because it retains only 28% of the reference yield variance. Every decision disagreement at the 70% and 80% levels is a MISSED loss, never a false alarm.",
  "caveats": [
    "No Gram Panchayat or Insurance Unit exists in this data; the real scheme decides at the IU, this simulates individual plots.",
    "The benchmark is the train-split mean, NOT a PMFBY Threshold Yield.",
    "No Sum Insured is available, so no monetary figure is computed.",
    "Verification is assumed to resolve a case to the reference value exactly, which overstates what a real crop-cutting experiment does.",
    "The reference itself is farmer-recalled yield, not a CCE measurement."
